Yashichi <devnull@127.0.0.1> writes:
> I have some questions not explicitly covered in the Artifacts spoiler, but
> derived from it. 
> 
> If I read correctly, alignments are adjusted only if the artifact is given
> by a god, not if wished for; thus a wish for magicbane will produce a
> neutral-aligned artifact no matter who wishes for it.

False. (I'm not sure what you're reading that into.) The adjustment
happens at the start of the game, so a character that started as a
chaotic Wizard who wishes for, finds, _or_ receives Magicbane will
find it to be chaotically aligned.

> It's impossible to wish for an alignment on an artifact,
> e.g. "blessed chaotic magicbane," correct?

Correct. "Nothing fitting that description exists in the game.",
for any attempt to specify an alignment on anything (except altars
in wizmode).

> Or is it possible to adjust the alignment on a non-intelligent
> artifact by wishing?

No.

> If all co-aligned and unaligned artifacts already exist in the game, will
> a god start drawing gifts from other alignments (subject to the lengthy
> 2/n+1 odds), and will those alignments be adjusted? Or will ze just "run
> out" of available gifts?

He'll run out, and sacrifice results that would be a gift will be a
luck boost instead.

> [I'm assuming for this purpose the player's quest
> object "exists" whether the player has done the quest or not.]

Well, it doesn't exist for artifact-gift purposes until you visit the
Quest goal level; it just isn't eligible to be given as a gift.
(SPFX_NOGEN, in source terms.)

